# Orbit Omni section QA (locked forward · scoped 2026-08-27)

**Omni is not the default film engine.** As of 27 Aug 2026: **Veo** does cinematic **world** plates in Google AI Studio; **Omni only** when Orbit the orange robot must move. Do **not** plan ~8–10 Omni plates per VO minute or Omni the whole Thursday film.

When Omni *is* used (the 1–2 Orbit beats), apply this QA. Pipeline overview: `orbit-omni-longform-playbook.mdc` · `00_Brand/Channel-Setup/OMNI_LONGFORM_PLAYBOOK.md`.

Historical Europa Parts **01–08** / Neutron minute builds taught these character and picture rules — keep the QA bar, drop the gen budget.

## Process

1. **World first:** AI Studio stills → Veo Fast money shots for science/world. Mute Veo audio.
2. **Omni only** for Orbit motion in inquisitive / story-narrative beats. Script QA → VO → Omni take(s) for those beats only → character picture QA.
3. **Ben UAT** on Orbit takes before locking. Regen only failed Orbit plates — do not re-Omni the world.
4. Keep VO-literal picture. World plates carry the science; Orbit is not wallpaper on every cut.

## Motion coverage (no “broken video” freezes)

1. **Never freeze-pad** (`tpad` / last-frame clone) to stretch short clips to VO length — it looks broken.
2. **Never loop / slow-mo** scenery (see `orbit-cutscene-no-reuse`).
3. **Stills-first economy:** stills + **2–3** Veo Fast (~8s) money shots carry the film. Do **not** “fix coverage” with Omni world plates.
4. Assembler must **fail** (or trim ≤~1s of VO) rather than freeze-extend picture.

## Character in the scene (when Orbit is on screen)

Reference feel: Orbit **turns**, you see **exhaust / propulsion**, he **flies off**. Reads as a character *in* the world, not a sticker.

1. **Orbit interacts with the scene** — bank/turn, push off, skim, tip, dive, react. Body language + motion sell presence.
2. **Readable agency:** soft underside glow as he moves; tiny bubble wake underwater OK. **Propulsion lock:** exactly **ONE** centered **bottom** underside glow. Forbidden: twin thrusters, left+right jets, rear+bottom dual exhaust, side engines, underwater **flames / fire plumes**.
3. **Camera treats him as subject** — parallax, enter/leave with intent — not locked dead-center hover for the whole take.
4. Prompts: concrete verb of interaction + continuous motion.
5. Reject plates where Orbit is a static ornament while the world does all the work — if he is not acting the line, cut him and use the world plate.
6. Travel beats: gaze / nose along **direction of travel** when moving.
7. Hang beat only when VO says he hangs — then a **tiny figure in the void**, not a foreground hero.

## Picture quality bar

1. **VO-literal** — when VO names an object, **cut to that object** (Neutron Star teaspoon vs mountains — gold beat). World does the science.
2. **Style:** premium **CGI 3D polish**. Reject 2D cartoon outlines / flat cel-shade when it breaks continuity.
3. **Env honesty:** underwater stays submerged; vacuum/space stays dry. Never ship space/surface with underwater bubble trails.
4. Tag plates `env: underwater | surface | space` and **gate water SFX** to underwater windows only.

## Single Orbit / single face (hard — Omni takes)

1. **Exactly one Orbit** in frame. Twin / clone / reflection / ghost = reject and regen.
2. **Exactly one face** — one front black visor with cream eyes + pupils. Reject second rear/side faceplate.
3. **Turns:** solid matte orange back (antenna stem + small hatch OK). No second visor mid-turn.
4. Spot-check start / mid / end before locking.
5. Do **not** I2V wide/acting plates from the full-frame identity still alone — attach a composition start frame at the correct scale (and no visor for back shots).
6. Eyes: cream/white **with dark pupils** — never blank solid white ovals.
7. **On-model or regen.** Knockoff (no visor, no arms, glowing belly, slit LEDs) is a different character.

## Clean vacuum

1. Space plates: **near-black**, a handful of faint pinpricks at most, **one** main distant star when the line needs it.
2. Reject dense star-noise / tiled white specks.

## Shot grammar (no formula approach)

1. **One VO idea → one literal image.** If VO and picture disagree, picture is wrong.
2. **Forbidden formula:** Orbit parked in a corner, destination opposite, fly toward it — as the default plate.
3. **Cap:** Orbit in **1–2** scenes per film only (inquisitive / story-narrative). At most one Orbit + distant-object establishing plate among those. The rest are world science plates.
4. **Subject follows the line.** Scenery-only plates are the default when Orbit is not who the line is about.
5. **Mute test before gen.** If the plate is pretty Orbit wallpaper under clever VO, rewrite it to the named object.

## Audio joins (Veo + rare Omni)

1. Mute/strip Veo baked audio under VO.
2. If Omni beds are present: assemble with paired **`xfade` + `acrossfade`** (~0.35–0.45s) or keep Omni SFX as quiet texture only under a **single continuous underscore**.
3. Do not treat plate native beds as the score.

## Prompt / gen hygiene

1. World: AI Studio Veo Fast, continuous motion, ~8s, silent. Orbit: Omni only when needed; single Orbit; single face; VO-literal verb; premium CGI; env lock.
2. Archive rejected plates (`_rejected_*`); bump asset version (`v02`/`v03`).
3. Historical Europa builders (`_gen_part0N_omni_*.py`) are **not** the default for new films.
